Subject: [PATCH 03508/11362] [outer-loop] ARC mechanism-parity: hazard world
 model was orphaned + duplicated an already-solved level; salvage as live-path
 move-pruner + reachability lint

Operator: "Is the mechanism we use in the outer loop the same one the live agent
uses to find solves? Otherwise we are wasting the effort." Audited it
(workflow arc-mechanism-parity-audit: 6 mappers -> synthesis -> adversarial
refutation; verdict different_mechanism, refutation synthesis_holds). The worry
was JUSTIFIED.

FINDING:
- The hazard-aware nav world model (arc_nav_world_model / HazardAwareNavWorldModel
  / escalating_deepen) was imported ONLY by scripts/experiments/* + its test --
  ZERO live-agent files.
- The live agent ALREADY deep-solves tu93 to L3 (registry L5) via the _tu93
  GameAdapter + verifier-routed best-first search (re-confirmed live: reached L3,
  reproduced, 2947 states, hand_verifier; a charger is just a dead-end the search
  prunes -- no model needed). So the hazard line re-solved an already-solved
  level via a mechanism the live agent never calls, and its omni rung was
  calibrated by an exhaustive real-env BFS a hidden-game agent cannot run.

SALVAGE (operator-chosen: efficiency-only, on the live path):
- arc_hazard_pruner.HazardMovePruner -- fits a hazard model from the SEARCH'S OWN
  observed deaths (no offline BFS), selects toward/omni by IN-SAMPLE
  observed-transition trust (conservative gate), no-ops when no hazard is present
  (safe for any game).
- OfflineSolver gains a move_pruner hook (all 3 branch modes); arc_loop_solve
  builds it by default (--no-hazard-prune to disable) and records pruner stats.
- A/B on tu93 L3 (results/arc_hazard_prune_ab_tu93.json): states_expanded
  2947 -> 2859 (-88 = exact pruned-move count), L3 solve PRESERVED (reproduced).
  Modest ~3% but real, and arc_nav_world_model is now reachable from the live
  path. Next step: feed the same pruner / HazardAwareNavWorldModel.engine into
  the SCORED E3AgentPolicy.plan_in_model path.

DISCIPLINE + LINT (operator-chosen):
- CLAUDE.md "ARC Live-Path Reachability Discipline" (registry-precheck before any
  per-game RE; every ARC solver/world-model module must be reachable from a live
  entrypoint).
- scripts/arc_orphan_solver_lint.py (pre-commit arc-orphan-solver-lint): computes
  the live import closure (handles relative + function-level imports), flags
  orphaned solver-like modules. Green (27 modules). Negative test confirms it
  catches re-orphaning of the pruner.

Adversarial review (FIX-FIRST) applied: corrected the "held-out" overclaim to
"in-sample observed-transition" (the trust is scored in-sample); taught the lint
to follow relative imports (so arc_world_model_synth is correctly reachable, not
falsely allow-listed) and to detect a NavWorldModel-consuming pruner directly;
verified no regression (dc22 no-ops cleanly, tu93 A/B reproduces exactly).

5 new pruner tests + 8 nav tests pass. mypy hook skipped (.venv/bin/mypy not
installed); ruff format+check + the orphan lint pass. Conductor STOPPED.

